::JOUR_U05_PRE_Q01::[MLA.JOUR.DIG.01] Source: Unit 5 Pretest Scenario. A student newsroom is preparing a digital feature package for the school website. The package may include a digital presentation, sequential images, accurate photos, revised article text, team production roles, an online publication page, and a deadline checklist. Some media parts are incomplete, some captions need checking, and the team must decide what is ready before publication. Question: Pretest Question 1: Which choice best supports responsible digital journalism before publication? {
~A. Publish first and check later#Not correct. Step 1: reread the embedded source instead of relying on a general preference. Step 2: locate the audience need, accuracy issue, digital tool, workflow, or publication requirement. Step 3: reject choices that weaken verification, visual accuracy, collaboration, sequence, deadline control, or publication readiness.
=B. Use accurate media, clear sequence, revision, teamwork, and deadline planning#Correct. Step 1: connect the decision to the MLA journalism standard shown in the item. Step 2: use the embedded source to verify the audience need, accuracy issue, digital tool, workflow, or publication requirement. Step 3: choose the option that protects credible, clear, publication-ready journalism.
~C. Choose the most colorful image even if outdated#Not correct. Step 1: reread the embedded source instead of relying on a general preference. Step 2: locate the audience need, accuracy issue, digital tool, workflow, or publication requirement. Step 3: reject choices that weaken verification, visual accuracy, collaboration, sequence, deadline control, or publication readiness.
~D. Let one person ignore the team workflow#Not correct. Step 1: reread the embedded source instead of relying on a general preference. Step 2: locate the audience need, accuracy issue, digital tool, workflow, or publication requirement. Step 3: reject choices that weaken verification, visual accuracy, collaboration, sequence, deadline control, or publication readiness.
}
